Carry the control requestId on native resume packets (extension 0.2.11)

A refused native resume had no ask identity, so a desktop host with
overlapping asks could not tell which ask it answers. The extension now
copies the control command's requestId verbatim onto type:"resume"
packets only; ordinary Start is unchanged. Hosts that do not use the
field ignore it (the resume schema stays additionalProperties:true).

- background.js: thread command.requestId to start(); set it only in
  the resume branch.
- request.schema.json: optional resume requestId, control domain.
- SPEC.md / RESUME-CAPTURE.md: document the field and the host rule
  (key a refused resume to its ask; a refusal without one records
  nothing on its own).
- Tests: VM test for string/integer ids and no id on ordinary Start;
  schema valid/invalid cases.
- manifest 0.2.10 -> 0.2.11.

